{
  "provider": "ElevenLabs",
  "speech": {
    "MARA:If you came for a room, the roof only leaks on the expensive side.": "mara-17d8bd0577cd2f96.mp3",
    "MARA:You have the key. Consider it payment for services to tidiness.": "mara-12a8b4a225585377.mp3",
    "MARA:An old chart. Bring back my brass tankard from the window table and you can have the key.": "mara-f5ee4285e5b5faaf.mp3",
    "MARA:Look before you pick things up. Then pick them up anyway. That seems to be how adventurers work.": "mara-1a03ec6f47a2a345.mp3",
    "MARA:My tankard! Here, take the chest key. The chart inside deserves some fresh air.": "mara-d012b8670f7b0c70.mp3",
    "ORIN:I haven’t lost my ship. I know exactly which ocean it’s in.": "orin-23b68f2b42a083d0.mp3",
    "ORIN:That chart marks Bellweather Shoal. Bring a boat. I’ve tried walking.": "orin-3f5f4f49b7022e70.mp3",
    "ORIN:Mara keeps a chart in that chest. She might part with the key if you help clear up.": "orin-4d483674d02a36d2.mp3",
    "ORIN:I got lost professionally until someone started paying me.": "orin-47092351414cf581.mp3",
    "NELL:A warm fire. A cold harbour. And absolutely no plan.": "nell-799301a574a1739a.mp3",
    "NELL:What’s in the sea chest?": "nell-a88b092e07bcefc5.mp3",
    "NELL:Any advice for a new arrival?": "nell-f0105939680a10aa.mp3",
    "NELL:Where should I start?": "nell-12ede28e9a8f1090.mp3",
    "NELL:How did you become a navigator?": "nell-f690f4316646a93c.mp3",
    "NELL:I’ll let you get back to it.": "nell-327b3e1b6c5910d5.mp3",
    "NELL:Brindle Quay. A city built on trade, tides, and the firm belief that somebody else will pay for repairs. Somewhere in these crooked streets, there must be work for a chartmaker.": "nell-8454e30c3fa8d771.mp3",
    "NELL:The Crooked Compass. Warm food, sailors with stories, and probably somebody who needs a map. An excellent place to start, particularly the warm food part.": "nell-e5b4d77f6e6c6ba2.mp3",
    "NELL:Quibble's Crossing connects the tavern streets to the harbour. Apparently the toll collector accepts sharp wit. At last, a currency I haven't already spent.": "nell-c4c8f0ffb7ea0622.mp3",
    "NELL:Here I am, at the Crooked Compass. Time to put this city on my map, and some supper on my plate.": "nell-0d8951b8428d290e.mp3",
    "NELL:I'm looking for surveying work.": "nell-c7cb5fab18c25958.mp3",
    "MARA:Then you've come to a place with water and disagreements.": "mara-b5f4e18672c66a13.mp3",
    "NELL:I brought a pencil.": "nell-eea92a1971827a4f.mp3",
    "MARA:Good. Most applicants bring another disagreement.": "mara-9500c30731a97742.mp3",
    "NELL:Does anyone need a chartmaker?": "nell-a3bb38fccfb7e991.mp3",
    "MARA:Everyone needs an accurate chart. Paying for one remains a minority interest. There's an old survey in that chest.": "mara-36782dee7c7f718a.mp3",
    "NELL:What's in the sea chest?": "nell-9933a2bbf7438bec.mp3",
    "NELL:Why don't you fetch the tankard?": "nell-38b0d3cb429a0925.mp3",
    "MARA:Because I have six customers' washing-up and one customer's ambition to encourage.": "mara-a3281edb4e1b2be3.mp3",
    "NELL:Can I keep the chart?": "nell-a195f6fd764445d1.mp3",
    "MARA:A chart ought to go somewhere. That one has mostly been under a blanket.": "mara-8f3577a085ef8c6c.mp3",
    "NELL:The markers don't agree with it.": "nell-869e665f3898c759.mp3",
    "MARA:Then check which one has changed. Old doesn't always mean wrong.": "mara-c615049824a169bb.mp3",
    "NELL:Do you know who made it?": "nell-f56bc8eb6ae321fe.mp3",
    "MARA:People who knew this harbour before it acquired an advertising budget.": "mara-000783208b89a957.mp3",
    "NELL:One tankard acquired. My career in piracy begins modestly.": "nell-459b203648fbfd47.mp3",
    "NELL:Locked. Perhaps Mara knows where the key is.": "nell-80ef50d6d470bac0.mp3",
    "NELL:A chart to Bellweather Shoal! Finally, a plan with a suspicious dotted line.": "nell-5f3ac56a20946ead.mp3",
    "NELL:These aren't decorative arrows. Someone measured the ebb channel.": "nell-8a284ecc6ba5e012.mp3",
    "NELL:But the new marker outside points across it. Either this chart has aged badly, or somebody's improved the water.": "nell-e44375f4318c6fac.mp3",
    "NELL:The key can stay on its hook. One less mystery in my pockets.": "nell-63be8915115b5d59.mp3",
    "NELL:The tankard is already taken care of.": "nell-5cb2c306d81687f4.mp3",
    "NELL:Wrong sort of tumbler.": "nell-a3a73892e7b489f9.mp3",
    "NELL:Too heavy. I'd have to chart a route just to lift it.": "nell-d5f35e86fb10d699.mp3",
    "NELL:A dramatic edit. I'll try a pencil first.": "nell-72a8a28a532eea4e.mp3",
    "NELL:An inspired combination. Unfortunately, the universe disagrees.": "nell-cd1c9696696a07e1.mp3",
    "NELL:Best leave that where it is.": "nell-797bebc9ab7009fb.mp3",
    "NELL:It is keeping its thoughts to itself.": "nell-ba9f63fa3b0768a7.mp3",
    "NELL:A fine brass tankard. Someone has engraved property of Mara underneath.": "nell-266a3c1c4e4007f8.mp3",
    "NELL:A sturdy sea chest. Its lock has survived more voyages than I have.": "nell-ea31658275e6fd33.mp3",
    "NELL:Shoreline observations wanted. Payment on verification. Below that: ship's cook wanted. Must distinguish salt from gunpowder.": "nell-eb1c8d6fa523f1c0.mp3",
    "NELL:A warehouse corner, a lighthouse, and some very new buoys. Out there: a thousand possible adventures. In here: better heating.": "nell-32015b475a5011fa.mp3",
    "NELL:The only member of this establishment with a reliable work ethic.": "nell-34ba6a5da6c46322.mp3",
    "NELL:Mara runs a tight ship. Particularly impressive for a building.": "nell-b5accc3aad2eb0b4.mp3",
    "NELL:A navigator who has misplaced his ship. Promising.": "nell-edbb178dbf4323fc.mp3",
    "NELL:Have you lost a ship?": "nell-ab68e13ebcb51d47.mp3",
    "ORIN:I haven't lost my ship. I know exactly which ocean it's in.": "orin-174d20709554b2c5.mp3",
    "NELL:Where did you last see it?": "nell-30aa52d76b99322a.mp3",
    "ORIN:At the berth indicated by an entirely official marker. It was a very reassuring marker.": "orin-e0b2ce7a1fece3c6.mp3",
    "NELL:Can you read this chart?": "nell-3b83d6de48ec7d4a.mp3",
